WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.000
Abraham: There has been a significant
growth in cyber criminality over the last

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.360
few years especially with ransomware.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.840
Breaches of personal data
leaves victims vulnerable to

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:11.569
fraud and puts lives at risk.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.910
Business is the main target although
phishing attacks on individuals

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.200
are increasing, however more people
are becoming aware of the threat.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.830
On a global scale governments and
nations are also at high risk of falling

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.959
victim to cyber crime in one way or
another and this affects everyone.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.140
Nicole: Cybercrime is a
violation of an individual's

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.539
privacy and their data security.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:40.680
They can be at risk of hacking, malware,
identity theft, financial fraud,

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:45.510
medical fraud, as well as interpersonal
cybercrime such as cyber bullying.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:51.449
Data is considered a commodity and is
a primary target of cybercriminals.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.620
It can be accessed illicitly if not
adequately protected by internet

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.420
security systems or given away to
scammers unwittingly by individuals

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.349
clicking onto bogus links and it can
be used to commit further cybercrimes.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.719
Abraham: Businesses are at risk
from Phishing, DDoS, and malware.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.929
Malware can include different subtypes
such as ransomware, trojans, worms, crypto

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.410
miners or spyware as a few examples.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.830
The attack type will often
depend on the type of business

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.460
and the technology they use.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.929
It will also be dependent on
what information the hacker

00:01:27.929 --> 00:01:29.799
wants to extract or attack.

00:01:30.559 --> 00:01:35.229
Cyber attacks can be, as we have already
discussed, by external or insider threats.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.580
Trojan malware enables hackers
to create a backdoor into the

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.559
business’ systems and access
business data and login credentials.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:47.849
Social engineering covers a broad range
of malicious cyber crimes manipulating

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.140
users into making security mistakes
or giving away sensitive information

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.510
or granting access to resources.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:59.580
Hackers can inject malicious code into
a website to gain access to information

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.810
and login details through keyloggers
and hacking a database of passwords.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.760
Nicole: There has been
a significant growth in

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.019
high-profile ransomware campaigns.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:13.640
Ransomware involves paying a hefty
fee for releasing their data,

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:18.080
however this does not always happen
even when the fee has been paid.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.780
There’s been a recent increase in
ransomware because companies have

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.800
started to use cyber insurance.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.769
If a company is affected by ransomware
then the insurance company will pay the

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:33.250
ransom, so cybercriminals know that it
is very likely they will get the money.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:37.259
There is, however, no guarantee
that the criminals will unencrypt

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.390
the data even after they are paid.

00:02:40.299 --> 00:02:41.445
Abraham: This can have a knock on
effect, an example of this is when the

00:02:41.445 --> 00:02:47.810
AXA insurance firm was ‘ransomwared’
in response to them publicly announcing

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.450
they will no longer offer ‘pay
out’ clauses for cyber insurance

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.040
It's common now to hear on the news
about cyber attacks from foreign

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.970
governments like North Korea, Russia
and China, but threats don't only

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.649
come from recognised countries.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.460
Cyber attacks at international
and national state level can

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:08.410
involve major organisations,
national infrastructure, political

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.829
parties, military, and governments.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.609
Nicole: The vulnerabilities for nations
are often the same and under the same

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:20.090
threats as businesses, but these can
take on much greater significance as they

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.359
can create consequences for everyone.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.430
The threats from nation states and
criminal groups are starting to become

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:31.020
blurred as some nation states use the
'facilities' provided by criminal groups

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.100
for their own 'state run' attacks.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.500
Many Russian-speaking cyber groups
are threatening UK interests, but

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:42.630
home-grown cyber criminals are also
becoming more sophisticated and

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.600
offering their services to others.

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:47.380
Abraham: The increasing ability
for purchasing 'cyber tools'

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.700
has enabled emerging threats
to become established quickly.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.020
Cyber security attacks have become
the new weapon of choice for many

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.920
nation states in the effort to
de-stabilise their opponents.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:02.560
Attacks and threats may be of a political
nature trying to skew the outcomes

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.060
of elections, financial gain, digital
surveillance to taking over of military

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:10.799
capabilities and rendering nations
helpless in the face of the threat.

